// 5:3. The image is 330 pixels high, so a unit is 110 pixels. The disc is 139.5 pixels across, radius
// 0.634, centered at (276, 146.5), which from the image's center is 2.55 and 1.332 here. Its bars
// change at 122 and 179 pixels down, so across the whole hoist they are 122:57:151.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Solo Polyamory Pride Flag"
  designer "NonMonoPrideFlags (DeviantArt)"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  date "2015-12-30"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20250425231629/https://www.deviantart.com/nonmonoprideflags/art/Solo-Polyamory-Pride-Flag-581141047"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20120213104012/http://www.isomedia.com/homes/jene/flag.html"
  note "NonMonoPrideFlags's DeviantArt post 'Solo Polyamory Pride Flag', as the Wayback Machine held it on 25 April 2025, says: 'This is my pride flag design for Solo Polyamory', an approach to polyamory that emphasizes agency and autonomy and doesn't seek tightly couple-centric relationships. It gives no color meanings, measurements or color values. The post is dated 30 December 2015 (UTC)."
  note "The disc holds the three colors of Jim Evans's polyamory flag (polyamory-pi in this collection), blue, red and black, in his order, in the designer's own shades. The post doesn't say so. The pi isn't used."
  note "The post's image is a JPEG of 541 by 330 pixels, 1.64:1, as are all this designer's flags of that month, so no deliberate proportion is clear. This file uses the common 5:3. The image is a cream field with a disc a little above the center and toward the fly, whose blue, red and black bars are 45, 57 and 37 pixels of its height, as measured above."
  note "The colors are read from the image's pixels, which are flat: cream #efe3af, blue #3f47cc, red #ed1b24 and black #000000."
  note "lgbtqia.wiki credits a solo polyamory flag to mogai-flags and illustrates it from elsewhere. That wasn't checked, and may be another design."
}
palette {
  cream "#efe3af"
  blue "#3f47cc"
  red "#ed1b24"
  black "#000000"
}
proportion hoist=3 fly=5

field cream

group {
  clip {
    disc {
      at fly=2.55 hoist=1.332
      radius 0.634
    }
  }
  bars blue red black {
    ratio 122 57 151
  }
}
